      "body": "I independently reproduced this on Windows before the competing fix, using pytest main `6a0de9be56365e75ff30d75cee9654739ca95f97`, Python 3.12.6, and the following minimal fixture-using doctest:\n\n```text\n# conftest.py\nimport pytest\n@pytest.fixture(autouse=True)\ndef auto_fixture():\n    yield\n\n# test_doctest.txt\n>>> 1 + 1\n2\n```\n\n`python -m pytest --doctest-glob=\"*.txt\" -q test_doctest.txt` passed (`1 passed`). The same run with `--fixtures-per-test` raised `AttributeError: 'DoctestItem' object has no attribute 'function'` in `_show_fixtures_per_test` and incorrectly exited 0. This confirms the report on Windows as well as Linux. I did not create a duplicate fix because #15055 already addresses the issue.",
